<title>USA: Blessings sees break even Q4 after-tax.</title>
<headline>Blessings sees break even Q4 after-tax.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT NEWS, Va. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blessings Corp said on Wednesday its fourth quarter net earnings after tax would be essentially break-even, compared to net income after tax of $0.17 per share in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Raw material costs were not expected to decline until 1997 and margins were projected to remain near historic lows through the quarter, Elwood Miller, president and chief executive officer, said.</p>
